# Testing Rule

- Treat tests as part of the implementation, not an afterthought.
- For behavior changes, add or update focused tests covering success and relevant failure paths.
- Prefer deterministic tests; avoid arbitrary sleeps and timing-dependent assertions where possible.
- For concurrency and networking, test cancellation, timeout, disconnect, malformed input, and resource cleanup where applicable.
- Run the narrowest relevant tests first, then the broader suite when practical.
- Before completion, run the repository's build and test workflow or document exactly why a check could not run.
- Never claim a test passed unless it was actually executed and passed.
